{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe runner attaches per-call usage to every result (`result[\"_usage\"]`, src/rebar/llm/runner.py:543) but Pass-1 discards it: passes.pass1_chunk, passes.pass1_container, and passes.pass1_isf return findings lists only, so BatchRunResult.outputs (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:167-176) carries no usage key and plan-review coverage.metrics has call counts but zero token totals for the most expensive pass (the gap is documented at src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:139-149). Per-criterion request counts are extracted (runner.py:_extract_usage) but never persisted, blocking data-driven criterion demotion decisions.\n\n## Approach\nrun_pass1 does not call runner.run directly — calls flow through _chunk -> sizing.pass1_with_ladder -> passes.pass1_chunk (and the container/ISF variants). So the usage is threaded through that chain: (1) passes.pass1_chunk, passes.pass1_container, and passes.pass1_isf change return type from list[dict] to (list[dict], dict) — findings plus the call's _usage dict; (2) sizing.pass1_with_ladder and pass1._chunk propagate the pair; (3) run_pass1 accumulates an aggregate sum plus a per-criterion map {llm_calls, requests, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens}; (4) the prerequisite finder runs in ProductionBatchRunner.run() (run_focused_finder is invoked there, not inside run_pass1), so its usage is merged into the aggregate in ProductionBatchRunner.run before emitting BatchRunResult.outputs[\"_usage\"]; (5) _attach_plan_review_metrics (src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:249+) folds the totals into coverage.metrics, and the per-criterion map is persisted into the REVIEW_RESULT sidecar coverage (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py). Alternative rejected: post-hoc parsing of the REBAR_USAGE_LOG JSONL — opt-in, not always present, and not keyed by criterion.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py, src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py, tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py (new, beside tests/unit/workflow/test_production_batch_runner.py).\n\n## Testing\nUnit with FakeRunner emitting stub _usage dicts: aggregate totals equal the sum over chunk, agent, container, ISF, and prerequisite calls; per-criterion map keys match the routed criteria; sidecar payload carries the map; a runner result without _usage degrades to zeros without error.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] After a review, coverage.metrics contains input/output/cache token totals that include Pass-1 and prerequisite calls (checked: `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py` summing FakeRunner stub usage).\n- [ ] The sidecar coverage carries a per-criterion usage map for every routed criterion (checked: sidecar payload unit test).\n- [ ] Missing _usage on any call degrades gracefully to zero contribution (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] Code-review finalize's existing token metrics are unchanged (checked: existing finalize tests pass)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785388165714980001,"uuid":"af8eb97c-8bc6-4bd7-bc6c-9848157a1a31"}